§ `ss 6, 11, 12 -- d031: admitted, then certified (replayed)`

-- Daniel admitted on 24 Aug 2020 holds a certificate (qualified); the same Daniel admitted but not yet certified (not).
#ASSERT `Am I a qualified entity` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Am I a qualified entity` TRUE FALSE FALSE

-- "Solicitor" on his letterhead before the certificate issues: presumed a representation (s 12(3)), and an offence (s 11(1)).
#ASSERT `Am I presumed to have represented that I am entitled to practise` TRUE

#ASSERT `May I say I am entitled to engage in legal practice` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: it would be an offence under Uniform Law s 11(1), up to 250 penalty units`

-- d030/d031: telling a client that Swan & Partners, a law practice, can act; and the same of an unqualified consultancy.
#ASSERT `May I say my firm is entitled to engage in legal practice` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the entity is a qualified entity`
#ASSERT `May I say my firm is entitled to engage in legal practice` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: it would be an offence under Uniform Law s 11(2), up to 50 penalty units`

§ `ss 6, 47 -- d031: Daniel's employee certificate`

#ASSERT `Am I a solicitor or a barrister` TRUE `as an employee of a law practice` EQUALS `a solicitor`
#ASSERT `Am I a solicitor or a barrister` TRUE `as or in the manner of a barrister only` EQUALS `a barrister`

-- As an employee (yes); as a principal (no); in-house before his first renewal (yes, s 47(4)(a)) and after it (no);
-- pro bono (yes, s 47(5)).
#ASSERT `Does my certificate let me practise as` `as an employee of a law practice` `as an employee of a law practice` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Does my certificate let me practise as` `as an employee of a law practice` `as a principal of a law practice` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Does my certificate let me practise as` `as an employee of a law practice` `as a corporate legal practitioner` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Does my certificate let me practise as` `as an employee of a law practice` `as a corporate legal practitioner` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Does my certificate let me practise as` `as an employee of a law practice` `as a volunteer or otherwise on a pro bono basis` TRUE FALSE

-- Swan & Partners with a partner authorised to receive trust money; a firm whose principals are not.
#ASSERT `May my firm receive trust money` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `May my firm receive trust money` FALSE FALSE

#ASSERT `Must I complete a reading program` `as or in the manner of a barrister only` FALSE FALSE FALSE

§ `ss 51, 86, 88, General Rules r 15 -- what Daniel must report`

#ASSERT `Must I report this to the Board` `I was convicted of an offence` `a WA speeding conviction with a fine` EQUALS `no: neither s 51 nor s 88 requires it`
#ASSERT `Must I report this to the Board` `I was convicted of an offence` `a WA drink-driving conviction with licence disqualification` EQUALS `yes: notify the Board in writing within 7 days (s 51(1))`
#ASSERT `Must I report this to the Board` `I was convicted of an offence` `a WA drink-driving conviction with a fine only` EQUALS `no: neither s 51 nor s 88 requires it`
#ASSERT `Must I report this to the Board` `I was charged with an offence` `an indictable fraud offence` EQUALS `yes: notify the Board in writing within 7 days (s 51(1))`
#ASSERT `Must I report this to the Board` `I was convicted of an offence` `an indictable fraud offence` EQUALS `not under s 51: it is an automatic show cause event, so give the Board a written notice within 7 days and a statement within 28 days (s 88)`
#ASSERT `Must I report this to the Board` `a bankruptcy-related event` `a WA speeding conviction with a fine` EQUALS `yes: notify the Board in writing within 7 days (s 51(1)); it is also an automatic show cause event, so give a written notice within 7 days and a statement within 28 days (s 88)`

#ASSERT `Is my notice in time` (Date 1 3 2029) (Date 8 3 2029)
#ASSERT NOT `Is my notice in time` (Date 1 3 2029) (Date 9 3 2029)

#ASSERT `What is the most I can be ordered to pay for breaching a condition`  EQUALS 100

